+ description: "Core dev loop with precision layer tightened to fixed advisory enums and explicit state shapes."
+ ## Layer Model
+ This skill has two layers:
+ - `core`: mandatory protocol for every round
+ - `precision`: optional enhancement layer for profiles, tuning, review cadence, metrics, and advisory scoring
+ The `precision` layer MUST NOT replace or weaken the `core` layer.
+ If `precision` is unavailable, the `core` layer MUST still run correctly.
+ 5. If precision is enabled, load project profile and tuning state.
+ 6. Develop the slice.
+ 7. Verify the slice.
+ 8. If precision is enabled, run configured precision checks.
+ 9. Evaluate continuation health.
+ 10. Write continuity state.
+ 11. Emit the human summary.
+ 12. Emit the machine-readable footer.
+ ## Precision Layer
+ The `precision` layer is optional.
+ The `precision` layer MAY add all of these capabilities:
+ - project-specific default commands and cadence through `profile.json`
+ - runtime tuning through `tuning.json`
+ - advisory review scheduling
+ - advisory metrics and trend tracking
+ - advisory scoring
+ - bounded hook execution only when explicitly enabled and allowed by repo policy
+ The `precision` layer MUST follow all of these rules:
+ - It MUST NOT replace the footer contract.
+ - It MUST NOT replace core stop rules.
+ - It MUST NOT silently change continuation priority.
+ - It MUST NOT imply automatic push or deploy by default.
+ - It MUST NOT stop or pause a loop by itself.
+ - It MUST degrade safely when unsupported.
+ - It MUST be profile-scoped when heuristics are language- or stack-specific.
+ Read precision behavior in [references/precision-overview.md](references/precision-overview.md).
+ If precision is enabled, additional state MAY be written through the precision templates defined in `templates/`.
+ The core layer does not define:
+ - scoring formulas as mandatory truth
+ - coverage heuristics as mandatory truth
+ - quality dashboards as mandatory truth
+ - automatic routing by score as mandatory truth
+ - automatic push behavior as mandatory truth
+ - repository-specific architecture heuristics as mandatory truth
+ Those concerns require explicit precision support or repository-specific policy.
